--TEST--
The four ways a `Core\Attributes` retrieval is refused where it is written (`rule:attributes/structural-retrieval` and `rule:attributes/retrieval-folds-while-checking`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
type Route = {path: string};

class Limits {
    public const int MAX = 5;
    // A constant whose own declaration folds to no value: `rule:classes/no-free-functions-or-constants` inlines a
    // class constant at every use site, and this compiler does not fold one
    // constant into another. That gap is `E0792` at a read, and it is the
    // whole of what `E0731` is left reporting below.
    public const int RELAY = Limits::MAX;
}

#[Route(path: "/a")]
#[Route(path: "/b")]
class Twice {}

// Attached to a class of its own, retrieved once: the payload of a site is
// type-checked once per retrieval that reaches it, so a second retrieval here
// would be a second copy of both diagnostics rather than a second mistake.
#[{code: Limits::RELAY}]
class Relay {}

// Accepted first, so a position that stops being accepted fails here rather
// than as a missing refusal: `all<T>` is what two matches are for.
array<Route> $ok = Core\Attributes::all<Route>(Twice::constructor);
echo Core\Arr::count($ok) as string, "\n";

// `rule:attributes/retrieval-folds-while-checking`: `get` answers at most one, and two is decided here rather than by a
// test run.
?Route $ambiguous = Core\Attributes::get<Route>(Twice::constructor);

// `rule:attributes/structural-retrieval`: retrieval is structural, so `T` has to be a shape.
?int $scalar = Core\Attributes::get<int>(Twice::constructor);

// The same rule: the target is a method reference, inspected where it is written —
// an anonymous function names no declaration.
callable $fn = fn (): int => 1;
?Route $computed = Core\Attributes::get<Route>($fn);

// `rule:attributes/retrieval-folds-while-checking`: the payload satisfies the shape, and the class constant it holds has no
// value of its own to compile in — the constant folder's gap surfacing at the
// one site that needs the value rather than the name.
?{code: mixed} $unfoldable = Core\Attributes::get<{code: mixed}>(Relay::constructor);

// `rule:attributes/structural-retrieval`: a *written* member name is checked against the target's real
// declarations. It has to be — the `null` a misspelling folds to is the answer
// a correct retrieval of an absent attribute gives, so nothing downstream
// could tell them apart. Only a computed name falls back to that empty result.
?Route $misspelled = Core\Attributes::get<Route>(Twice::constructor, "path");
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0792]: `Limits::RELAY` has no compile-time value to inline
   --> case.nvs:20:10
   |
20 | #[{code: Limits::RELAY}]
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this constant's declaration folds to no value
   = help: a class constant is copied into every place that uses it, so its value must be known when the program compiles. Write it as a number, a string, or an array of them. This compiler cannot yet do that for another class's constant, an enum case or `Foo::class`, alone or inside an array. Write the value out here, or move it to a `static` property that the class sets

error[E0731]: this attribute satisfies the retrieved shape, but holds a value with no compile-time form
   --> case.nvs:20:10
   |
20 | #[{code: Limits::RELAY}]
   |          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no constant form
   = help: the compiler replaces the call with the attribute's value, so every part of the value must be a constant. A constant here has no value the compiler can compute (`E0792`). Write the value here, or give that constant a literal value

error[E0728]: `Twice::constructor` has 2 attribute payloads that match this shape
   --> case.nvs:30:21
   |
30 | ?Route $ambiguous = Core\Attributes::get<Route>(Twice::constructor);
   |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `get` answers at most one
   = help: write `Core\Attributes::all<T>(…)`, which returns every match

error[E0729]: `Core\Attributes::get` retrieves a shape, and `int` is not one
   --> case.nvs:33:16
   |
33 | ?int $scalar = Core\Attributes::get<int>(Twice::constructor);
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `int` written here
   = help: an attribute matches when its value has every field of the shape `T`. Write `T` as a shape `{...}`, or as a `type` alias of a shape

error[E0730]: a `Core\Attributes` retrieval names no declaration
   --> case.nvs:38:48
   |
38 | ?Route $computed = Core\Attributes::get<Route>($fn);
   |                                                ^^^ this is not a declaration reference
   = help: write a method reference: `Foo::bar` for a method, or `Foo::constructor` for the class itself. A property or parameter name in quotes can follow it

error[E0798]: a `Core\Attributes` retrieval names `$path`, which `Twice` does not declare
   --> case.nvs:49:70
   |
49 | ?Route $misspelled = Core\Attributes::get<Route>(Twice::constructor, "path");
   |                                                                      ^^^^^^ no parameter or property of that name
   = help: a misspelled name would give `null` or an empty array. A correct name with no attribute gives the same result, so the name is checked here. Correct the name

error: aborting due to 6 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
